WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.534
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.669
-Good to see you, man.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.137
-I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.905
I'm so excited about this.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.140
People are going to freak out.
It's so good.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.709
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:13.146
-Before we get into this,
you just wrapped your tour.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.548
It's called
"The Unfortunate Return

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.550
of the Ridiculously
Self-Indulgent

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:21.054
Ill-Advised Vanity Tour."
-Yes.

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.922
-But you just wrapped up
at Carnegie Hall.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.524
-Yes, oh, my goodness.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.126
-What was that like?
-So emotional.

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.994
-I mean, it was a six-month tour
ending at Carnegie Hall

00:00:28.994 --> 00:00:30.396
just this last Saturday night.

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:33.365
And the whole six months
I'm a little nervous.

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:34.801
You know, I'm kind of
freaked out, 'cause, you know,

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.169
Carnegie Hall, one of the most
prestigious venues in the world.

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:38.838
-Yeah.
-Bucket-list item for me.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.439
So the whole six months
I'm like,

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:42.108
"Got to get ready
for Carnegie Hall."

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.909
-Yeah.
-And we get next to the --

00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:46.179
A couple days before,
I'm just starting to freak out.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.746
And then the day of the show,
I'm thinking,

00:00:47.746 --> 00:00:50.383
"Okay, I've just done 128 shows.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.653
It's just another show.
It's just another show."

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.854
And then I get
inside the building,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.489
and I walk down the hall
to the dressing room,

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.559
and there's giant pictures of,
you know, Judy Garland

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.627
and Frank Sinatra
and The Beatles.

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:04.330
And my brain starts screaming,
"I don't belong here!

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.066
I don't belong here!"
-"I don't belong here at all."

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.302
Oh, my gosh.
-It went great, it went great.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.803
-Questlove was there

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:13.039
and actually said it was one of
the best shows he's ever seen.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.607
-Oh, thank you.
-Yeah, it was amazing.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.142
Congratulations on that.
-Thank you.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:19.645
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:22.815
-I've been talking about this
with different people

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:25.050
that have been in the movie
and made cameos in the movie.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.819
And Daniel Radcliffe was here.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:27.953
But I want to talk about this.

00:01:27.953 --> 00:01:30.255
This is "Weird:
The Al Yankovic Story."

00:01:30.255 --> 00:01:32.224
It is a biopic about your life.

00:01:32.224 --> 00:01:34.393
-Yes.
100% accurate.

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:36.229
-Yeah, right.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:39.798
It is gating rave, rave,
rave reviews on this.

00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:43.436
It's clever.
It's musical.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.938
It's smart.
It's funny, obviously.

00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:49.241
But let me set the tone
for the movie.

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:50.276
Right, this will set the tone.
-Okay.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.377
-This is log line.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.612
"Daniel Radcliffe
is Weird Al Yankovic

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:55.881
in the unexaggerated true story

00:01:55.881 --> 00:01:59.452
about the greatest musician
and sex symbol of our time."

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.254
-Yes.
-That's the log line.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.455
-That pretty much wraps it up.
-That wraps it up there, yeah.

00:02:03.455 --> 00:02:06.492
How does the idea of a biopic
come to you?

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.361
Did you think
you would ever do this?

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:11.130
-It came from Eric Appel,
who directed the movie.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.532
-Fantastic job, by the way.
-Amazing. His first feature.

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:15.301
-He crushed this one.
-Yeah.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.270
But he directed the original
Funny or Die video

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.805
that this is based on,
which he did in 2010,

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:21.874
so this is 12 years
in the making.

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:24.510
And the original video basically
is sort of like the --

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.746
you know, where the whole thing
sprang from.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:29.081
Aaron Paul starred in
the original version of me.

00:02:29.081 --> 00:02:30.750
And Olivia Wilde played Madonna.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.385
But we thought --
at the time, it was like,

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:33.686
"Oh, this is
a funny little video."

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.621
And it went viral.
And I play it in my live shows.

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:37.390
And everybody was like,
"When is the movie coming out?"

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:40.326
And I'd say, "It's just a gag.
It's just a joke."

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.827
But then after nine years
of that,

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:44.931
I said,
"Maybe we should do a movie."

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.132
-Yeah.
-So we did. Yeah.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.199
-I mean, it's unbelievable.

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:49.035
Did you know
it was Daniel Radcliffe

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.003
was gonna be the person
to play you?

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:52.471
-He was our number-one choice.

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:54.607
And, yeah, I mean,
even though Daniel --

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.142
I think he said on your show
last night,

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:58.410
he's not an exact physical
doppelganger for me.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.646
There's not a huge
physical resemblance there.

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:02.548
-No, you look
completely different.

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:03.850
-Well, yeah, kind of.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.884
But we just felt like
he had the right energy.

00:03:05.884 --> 00:03:07.754
You know, and we thought
maybe he'd go for it

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.922
'cause famously, after
the "Harry Potter" series,

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:11.890
he's chosen a lot of --
I'm not going to say weird,

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:13.993
but a lot of different,
you know, kind of --

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.828
He played a flatulent corpse

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.696
and a guy that grows horns
out of his head.

00:03:17.696 --> 00:03:19.231
Maybe he could be Weird Al.

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:21.567
-Yeah, he does
make great choices.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.069
-And also,
he's got the right energy

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:25.738
and the right attitude
and the chops.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.707
I mean, he does --
he's great at comedy.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.274
He's great at drama.
And we want--

00:03:29.274 --> 00:03:31.944
It's obviously a comedy,
but we wanted it --

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:34.246
We didn't want it to play
like a comedy.

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:36.348
We wanted to play
like a very serious,

00:03:36.348 --> 00:03:38.585
you know, Oscar-bait
Hollywood biopic.

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:41.320
-Yeah, maybe that's what's
so brilliant about it.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.290
He plays it so serious
and perfectly funny,

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.360
but, I mean, he's a good actor
and good chops.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.397
And Evan Rachel Wood, by
the way, plays Madonna in this.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.666
And I'm telling you guys,
you're going to freak out.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:54.733
She's unbelievable.

00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:56.202
-I'm so sad that
we didn't have her sing.

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.170
'Cause when she came
on your show and sang Madonna,

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.771
Eric and I were both, like,
watching the show going,

00:03:59.771 --> 00:04:01.507
"Why didn't we have her sing
in the movie?"

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.576
-Yeah, she doesn't sing in --
Yeah, exactly.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.144
-But Daniel was saying,

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.712
"We also couldn't afford
any Madonna songs."

00:04:06.712 --> 00:04:08.948
-True, true.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.383
But you know what was funny?

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.251
There was a --
You posted this.

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:13.686
There's actually
a Google search.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.654
You said, "It amuses me
to no end that this is currently

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:17.423
the number-three Google search
under my name."

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.926 line:0%
If you search "Weird Al," number
three is Weird Al and Madonna.

00:04:20.926 --> 00:04:24.163 line:0%
-Yeah, because on the trailer,
which had just come out,

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.898
it's obvious that
there's something going on

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.199
with me and Madonna,
so everybody was like,

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:28.700
"Did that really happen?

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.469
Did Weird Al and Madonna
have a thing?"

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.638
-Yeah, what was the story
with Madonna?

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:35.274
What part is truth,
or do you want to say?

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.576
-Well, there are a few
little nuggets of truth

00:04:37.576 --> 00:04:39.178
sprinkled throughout the biopic.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.379
The only time we actually --

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:42.548
Our relationship is platonic,
by the way.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:45.551
The only time I actually met her
was in 1985.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:48.387
I talked to her for maybe
like 45 seconds backstage.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:49.688
So that's the extent
of the relationship.

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:50.923
-And she's in the whole movie.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.591
-Oh, she's a huge part
of the movie.

00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:54.260
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:57.596
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:57.596 --> 00:05:01.033
-It's so good.
It's so good.

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:04.070
Another thing I loved about it,
and this is, I know, true

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.205
'cause I'm a superfan
of Weird Al,

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:09.608
is the Yankovic bump is what
they call it in the business.

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:12.278
If Weird Al does a parody
of your song,

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:14.646
your actual sales go up.

00:05:14.646 --> 00:05:16.349
-That's an actual thing.
-That is true.

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:17.850
-So we use that in the movie,
as well,

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.418
but, of course,
we exaggerate it a bit.

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:21.687
Madonna sort of becomes like
the "villain" in the movie.

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:25.123
She, like, does everything
she can to calculatedly get me

00:05:25.123 --> 00:05:26.725
to do a parody of her new single

00:05:26.725 --> 00:05:29.762
so she can get
that Yankovic bump, you know.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:31.864
-But it happened with Nirvana.
-Nirvana, yeah.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:35.100
In fact, after my "Smells Like
Nirvana" parody came out,

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.003
we got a phone call from
Nirvana's record label saying,

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:39.471
"Thank you.

00:05:39.471 --> 00:05:42.141
Because of your parody, we just
sold an extra million units

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.409
of 'Nevermind.'"

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.444
-A million units
because of your --

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:46.745
-Yeah, that's what he said,
yeah.

00:05:46.745 --> 00:05:48.614
[ Applause ]

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:51.484
-And I think Kurt got
the phone call in this building.

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:53.252
-At "Saturday Night Live," yeah.
-"Saturday Night Live," yeah.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.454
-Yeah, 'cause we couldn't
track down the right people

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:56.822
from his record label
to get the blessing.

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:58.690
And finally I was like,
"I'm just going to call him

00:05:58.690 --> 00:05:59.959
on the set
of 'Saturday Night Live.'"

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.727
And he picked up the phone.

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:04.896
It's an old story, but basically
I said I wanted to do a parody.

00:06:04.896 --> 00:06:06.498
And he said, "It's going to be
about food?"

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:08.066
I said, "No, it's about how

00:06:08.066 --> 00:06:09.568
nobody can understand
your lyrics,"

00:06:09.568 --> 00:06:10.737
and he went, "Great."

00:06:10.737 --> 00:06:12.104
-He loved it.

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:14.773
The soundtrack, by the way,
is massive.

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:16.976
This is an amazing soundtrack.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.878
46 songs?

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:21.546
-Well, it's not all me.

00:06:21.546 --> 00:06:23.382
It's the whole orchestral score.

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:25.017
And it's a bunch
of re-recorded parodies.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:27.186
I got to re-record,
"Another One Rides the Bus,"

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:29.054
"My Bologna,"
"I Love Rocky Road"

00:06:29.054 --> 00:06:31.123
and "Amish Paradise"
and "Like a Surgeon."

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:32.758
So it was weird to go back
into the studio

00:06:32.758 --> 00:06:34.259
like 40 years later...

00:06:34.259 --> 00:06:36.095
-And do it again?
-...and do it again, yeah.

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:39.198
-But how much -- I mean,
how much music is this?

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:43.102
It's a lot of music.
-It's 78 minutes and 17 seconds.

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:45.571
-Gosh.
I mean, I --

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.006
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:51.310
I don't say this just to say it,
but I love the movie so much,

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.379
and all -- when you see it,
you're going to --

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:55.781
I think there's awards buzz
around this movie.

00:06:55.781 --> 00:06:58.150
That would be fantastic to see.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:01.353
-I hope I get a Razzie.
-No, no, not a Razzie.

00:07:01.353 --> 00:07:03.789
I'm telling you, man,
it's so well done.

00:07:03.789 --> 00:07:05.624
You're in the movie.

00:07:05.624 --> 00:07:07.059
Can you tell everyone
who you play?

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.961
'Cause you're not --
Clearly you are Weird Al,

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.963
but you can't play Weird Al.
-I sort of play the same part

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:12.531
that I played in the original
Funny or Die video.

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:15.734
I play the president
of my record label

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:18.371
who turns Weird Al down
in the movie.

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:21.207
-Yeah, and Will Forte
is in this scene, as well.

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:22.875
-Yes, indeed.
-Man, he's unbelievably funny.

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:25.110
-Amazing.
-There's so many cameos in this.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.112
And every like three seconds,
you'll see somebody else.

00:07:27.112 --> 00:07:28.714
You're like, "What?
Oh, my gosh."

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:29.915
Legend upon legend.

00:07:29.915 --> 00:07:32.017
It's just so enjoyable and fun,

00:07:32.017 --> 00:07:34.019
and I want to
show everyone a clip.

00:07:34.019 --> 00:07:37.022
Here's Weird Al Yankovic in
"Weird: The Al Yankovic Story."

00:07:37.022 --> 00:07:38.190
Take a look.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.959
Look, kid, if you really
have your heart set

00:07:40.959 --> 00:07:45.598
on doing this stupid music,
maybe write more than one song.

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:47.366
-Yeah, all the biggest
musical acts

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:49.668
have more than one song
in their catalogue.

00:07:49.668 --> 00:07:50.903
-That's very true.

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:53.238
And also, get out in front
of a live audience.

00:07:53.238 --> 00:07:56.141
Any audience, any stage,
just get out there,

00:07:56.141 --> 00:07:58.477
build up your chops,
and who knows?

00:07:58.477 --> 00:08:01.714
Maybe someday we'll talk again.

00:08:01.714 --> 00:08:05.117
-But don't count on it,
because you truly suck.

00:08:05.117 --> 00:08:06.285
-Right.

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:07.686
-Okay.

00:08:07.686 --> 00:08:09.254
-That's exactly right.

00:08:09.254 --> 00:08:11.190
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.359
I can't wait.
You know I love you.

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:14.693
You're one of my favorites.
-Thank you.

00:08:14.693 --> 00:08:16.395
-Weird Al Yankovic, everybody.

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:19.931
"Weird: The Al Yankovic Story"
is available for free

00:08:19.931 --> 00:08:23.369
exclusively on The Roku Channel
this Friday.

